      "reasoning": "Interesting options. I already have a Forest in hand for turn 3, so I don't need a land. Let me think about what I want to draw:\n\
\n\
- **Elvish Rejuvenator** (3 mana, 1/1 Elf, ramps a land) - decent but small body\n\
- **Primeval Herald** (4 mana, 3/1 Elf Scout, trample, ramps on ETB and attack) - powerful but 4 mana\n\
- **Forest** - just a land\n\
\n\
I want to curve out well. Turn 3 I want to play either Dwynen's Elite (2 mana, gets token with Silhana on board) + something, or Elvish Archdruid (3 mana). Actually, I already have great 2 and 3 drops in hand. Let me put a Forest on top to ensure I hit my land drop next turn if I want to play Archdruid turn 3 AND Dwynen's Elite... wait, I already have a Forest in hand.\n\
\n\
For turn 3 with 3 lands, I can play Elvish Archdruid or Dwynen's Elite. Turn 4 I want 4 lands for bigger plays. Primeval Herald at 4 mana with trample and land ramp is strong. But I might want the Forest to guarantee my 4th land drop.\n\
\n\
Actually - I'll put Forest on top. Guaranteeing my 4th land for turn 4 is more important, and I have plenty of creatures in hand already.",
