      "reasoning": "Turn 3! Opponent has 2 Forests and 7 cards in hand but no creatures. I drew the Forest I set up. \n\
\n\
Now I need to think about sequencing. I have 3 mana available (2 untapped + 1 land drop). My options:\n\
\n\
1. Play Forest → Cast Elvish Archdruid (1GG) - gives Silhana Wayfinder and itself +1/+1, and taps for mana equal to elves\n\
2. Play Forest → Cast Dwynen's Elite (1G) - gets a 1/1 token since I control Silhana Wayfinder (an Elf), then still have 1 mana open\n\
3. Play Forest → Cast Ghirapur Guide (2G)\n\
\n\
The best play is Elvish Archdruid. It makes my Silhana Wayfinder a 3/2, and next turn with 4 lands + Archdruid's tap ability, I can dump my whole hand. Archdruid on curve is the strongest elf play.",
