      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "New 2/2 elf token created! Now I have 6 elves total. Archdruid taps for 6 mana. My board is massive.\n\
\n\
Now for combat. Opponent has Turntimber Basilisk (2/1 deathtouch, summoning sickness). I can attack with:\n\
- Dwynen's Elite (3/3)\n\
- Ghirapur Guide (4/3) \n\
- Silhana Wayfinder (3/2)\n\
- Elvish Archdruid (2/2) - but I might want to keep this back for mana\n\
\n\
The Basilisk has summoning sickness so it can't block. Wait, summoning sickness only prevents attacking and tapping - it CAN block! Deathtouch means it'll kill anything it blocks.\n\
\n\
If I attack with everything except the tapped token and new token (sick), opponent can block one creature with Basilisk. I should use Ghirapur Guide's ability to make one of my creatures unblockable. \n\
\n\
Let me save the Guide ability for after blocks. Actually, Ghirapur Guide's ability costs {2}{G} and makes target creature unblockable if defender has no green creatures... wait, let me check.",
