      "reasoning": "Excellent! Opponent is at 7 life! They blocked Silhana Wayfinder with the Basilisk (deathtouch killed it, but the other 7 damage got through - 14 → 7). They played Garruk's Gorehorn (7/3) with summoning sickness.\n\
\n\
I drew Wildheart Invoker (4/3, costs {2}{G}{G}). Its activated ability costs 8 mana for +5/+5 and trample - that's a lot.\n\
\n\
My board: 5 elves (Archdruid, Dwynen's Elite, Ghirapur Guide, 2 Elf Warrior Tokens). Archdruid taps for 5 green.\n\
\n\
Let me think about lethal:\n\
- Current attackers: Dwynen's Elite (3/3), Ghirapur Guide (4/3), and potentially Archdruid (2/2) = 9 damage. But Gorehorn (7/3) can block.\n\
- If I cast Wildheart Invoker (another elf), Archdruid would tap for 6. All creatures get +1/+1 from Archdruid having 6 elves... wait, Archdruid gives OTHER elves +1/+1 per elf you control. So with 6 elves, each other elf gets +6/+6? No wait - Archdruid gives \"Other Elf creatures you control get +1/+1 for each Elf you control.\" \n\
\n\
Wait, let me re-read Archdruid.",
