      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "OK so Archdruid gives +1/+1 static (not scaling). Currently 5 elves, taps for 5 green. My creatures are buffed:\n\
- Dwynen's Elite: base 2/2 → 3/3 (+1/+1 from Archdruid)\n\
- Ghirapur Guide: base 3/2 → 4/3\n\
- Elf Warrior Tokens: base 1/1 → 2/2 each\n\
\n\
If I cast Wildheart Invoker (an elf), that's 6 elves total. Archdruid still gives +1/+1 (the buff doesn't scale with elf count, only the mana does). So Invoker would be 4/3 base → 5/4 with Archdruid.\n\
\n\
Let me plan: Cast Wildheart Invoker ({2}{G}{G}), then activate Presence of Gond token, then go to combat.\n\
\n\
Available mana: 5 lands + Archdruid (5 green) = 10 mana. Invoker costs 4. That leaves 6 mana. Guide ability costs 3, could use twice. Or activate the token engine.\n\
\n\
Actually, opponent is at 7. Their Gorehorn is 7/3 with summoning sickness - it can block. If I can get 7 damage through, I win.\n\
\n\
Potential attackers after casting Invoker: Dwynen's Elite (3/3), Ghirapur Guide (4/3), both Elf Warrior Tokens (one is tapped from Presence of Gond, one might be available). Wait, one token is enchanted with Presence of Gond. If I tap it to make a token, it can't attack.\n\
\n\
Let me activate Presence of Gond token first (free), then cast Wildheart Invoker, then use Guide ability.\n\
\n\
Attackers would be: Dwynen's Elite (3/3), Ghirapur Guide (4/3), one Elf Warrior Token (2/2), plus the new token will have summoning sickness. Invoker will have summoning sickness too.\n\
\n\
Total attackable: 3 + 4 + 2 = 9 power. Opponent has Gorehorn (7/3) to block. If they block Ghirapur Guide (4/3), 5 damage gets through (opponent to 2). If they block Elite, 6 gets through. If they block token, 7 gets through (lethal!).\n\
\n\
So I need to make my biggest creatures unblockable. Use Guide ability twice:\n\
- Make Ghirapur Guide unblockable by power 2 or less (Gorehorn is power 7, so this doesn't help!)\n\
\n\
Wait - Gorehorn is 7/3. Guide's ability only prevents blocking by creatures with power 2 or less. The Gorehorn has power 7, so Guide's ability is useless here!\n\
\n\
OK so the opponent will block the biggest creature with Gorehorn. If they block Guide (4 power), 5 damage through. If they block Elite (3 power), 6 through. Either way, not lethal.\n\
\n\
Unless... I use Wildheart Invoker's activated ability! It costs 8 mana: target creature gets +5/+5 and trample. If I buff Ghirapur Guide to 9/8 with trample, and Gorehorn blocks it, 6 damage tramples over (9-3=6), plus Elite (3) + Token (2) = 11 unblocked. WAY more than lethal.\n\
\n\
But I need to cast Invoker (4 mana) AND activate it (8 mana) = 12 mana. I have 5 lands + Archdruid (5 with current elves, or 6 if I have 6 elves after casting Invoker). So after casting Invoker: 5 lands left untapped (if I use Archdruid for casting) minus lands used... Let me think more carefully.\n\
\n\
Actually, Invoker has summoning sickness so I can't activate its ability the turn it comes down! Wait - the ability targets a creature, it doesn't have tap in its cost. Let me re-check.\n\
\n\
\"{8}: Target creature gets +5/+5 and gains trample until end of turn.\" - No tap required! Just 8 mana. So I CAN activate it the turn it comes down.\n\
\n\
Mana plan:\n\
1. Tap Archdruid (currently 5 elves = 5 green)\n\
2. Tap 5 lands = 5 more green\n\
3. Total: 10 green mana\n\
4. Cast Wildheart Invoker: 4 mana. 6 remaining.\n\
5. Activate Invoker: 8 mana. Need 8 but only have 6. NOT ENOUGH.\n\
\n\
Hmm. What if I make a token first with Presence of Gond? That adds an elf, making Archdruid tap for 6.\n\
\n\
1. Activate Presence of Gond (tap enchanted token → create new token)\n\
2. Now 6 elves. Archdruid taps for 6.\n\
3. Tap Archdruid (6) + 5 lands (5) = 11 mana\n\
4. Cast Invoker: 4 mana. 7 remaining.\n\
5. Activate Invoker: 8 mana. Still need 8 but only have 7. One short!\n\
\n\
Argh. What about not casting Invoker and just attacking?\n\
\n\
Without Invoker: 5 elves, attack with Dwynen's Elite (3/3), Ghirapur Guide (4/3), and maybe one Elf Warrior Token (one is tapped from Gond). Total: 3+4+2 = 9 power. Opponent blocks one with Gorehorn. Best case 7 through (if they block token). But they'll block the biggest threat.\n\
\n\
Actually wait - if I don't cast Invoker, I have 11 mana (after Gond activation). I can activate Invoker's ability... no, Invoker isn't on the battlefield yet.\n\
\n\
Alternative: Just attack and use Guide's ability to dodge blocks. But Gorehorn has power 7, so Guide's ability doesn't help against it.\n\
\n\
Let me just attack with my team. Dwynen's Elite (3), Guide (4), and one token (2) = 9 damage. They block Guide with Gorehorn, so 5 gets through. Opponent goes to 2. They're dead next turn because they can't block everything.\n\
\n\
Actually wait - if I make a token first AND keep the non-enchanted token available to attack:\n\
\n\
Let me check which tokens can attack. p39 is the enchanted token (I'll tap it for Gond). p48 is the other token - can it attack?\n\
\n\
Looking at the board state: both tokens are 2/2, one is the Gond-enchanted one. Neither has summoning sickness listed currently. So p48 can attack!\n\
\n\
Attackers: Dwynen's Elite (3/3), Ghirapur Guide (4/3), Elf Warrior Token p48 (2/2), and even Archdruid (2/2) if I don't need mana. That's 3+4+2+2 = 11 power. But I need Archdruid for mana if I want to activate Guide's ability.\n\
\n\
Hmm, let me just go with the straightforward plan: make a token, cast Invoker, attack with what's available.\n\
\n\
After casting Invoker with summoning sickness, my attackers are: Elite (3/3), Guide (4/3), Token p48 (2/2) = 9 power. Gorehorn blocks one. Best case 7 through = lethal if they block the 2/2 token. But opponent will block the 4/3 Guide, leaving only 5 through.\n\
\n\
OR: Don't cast Invoker, tap Archdruid for mana, use floating mana for Guide activations, and attack. \n\
\n\
Actually, can I activate Guide's ability on Dwynen's Elite and itself, then attack? Gorehorn has power 7, so the ability doesn't matter against Gorehorn. The ability only stops power 2 or less from blocking.\n\
\n\
I think the best play is:\n\
1. Make a token with Presence of Gond\n\
2. Cast Wildheart Invoker (grows the elf army)\n\
3. Attack with Elite, Guide, and Token p48\n\
4. Opponent blocks one, takes 5-7 damage, goes to 0-2\n\
5. Next turn is lethal regardless\n\
\n\
Let me execute this plan.",
