      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "OK, so Archdruid tapped for 6 green (6 elves), Thriving Grove and Forest tapped for 2 more = 8 green total. Invoker costs 4, so 4 mana floating. Plus 2 untapped Forests = 6 mana available.\n\
\n\
Wait - but Invoker isn't on the battlefield yet (it's on the stack). I can't activate its ability until it resolves. After it resolves and I have 6 mana remaining... but Invoker's ability costs 8. Not enough.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but wait. When Invoker resolves, I'll have 7 elves. But Archdruid is already tapped. So the extra elf count doesn't help for mana this turn.\n\
\n\
OK, so I can't use Invoker's ability this turn. Let me just let everything resolve and go to combat. The 4/3 Invoker (with Archdruid buff = 5/4) will have summoning sickness though.\n\
\n\
Let me pass and head to combat.",
