      "decision_index": 92,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Blocked Silhana Wayfinder (3/2) with deathtouch Turntimber Basilisk instead of Ghirapur Guide (4/3). Ghirapur Guide is the highest-power attacker and has an ability that makes creatures unblockable by power 2 or less, making it the most dangerous creature on the opponent's board. Blocking it saves 1 more life (take 6 instead of 7) and removes a more threatening creature.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked Silhana Wayfinder with Turntimber Basilisk",
      "better_line": "Block Ghirapur Guide (4/3) with Turntimber Basilisk to kill the biggest threat with deathtouch, saving 1 life and removing the most dangerous creature and its unblockable ability.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 146,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 99,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Opponent is at 7 life with no untapped creatures (Gorehorn is summoning sick). All of Opus Brewer's creatures can attack for 13 total damage - lethal. Activating Presence of Gond to tap a 2/2 token is unnecessary and reduces available attackers, though remaining creatures still deal 11 which is still lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Presence of Gond on Elf Warrior Token (tapping it) before combat, reducing attack force by 2 power.",
      "better_line": "Go directly to combat and attack with all creatures for 13 damage lethal. No precombat actions needed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 169,
      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "decision_index": 109,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 2 life with an empty board facing multiple enemy creatures, GPT53C Teach passed without casting Rampaging Growth, which would create a 4/3 reach blocker that could survive to block next turn. The opponent has multiple attackers (Dwynen's Elite 3/3, Elf tokens 2/2, Wildheart Invoker 5/4) — without any blockers, the next attack is almost certainly lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells, leaving the board completely empty at 2 life.",
      "better_line": "Cast Rampaging Growth (4 mana) to create a 4/3 Insect creature with reach and haste as a blocker. This is the only way to potentially survive the opponent's next combat. Could also have sequenced Garruk's Uprising first if mana allowed, but Rampaging Growth alone is critical for survival.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 194,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 122,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 2 life facing lethal next turn, GPT53C Teach passed on casting Rampaging Growth which could create a 4/3 haste creature. Combined with Hunter's Insight (3 mana) on the 4/3 attacker into a mostly-tapped board, this would draw 4 cards - the best and possibly only chance to find answers to survive. With 6 untapped lands (4 for Growth + the new land + 2 remaining = 3 available for Insight), this line was fully castable.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting Rampaging Growth, effectively giving up on finding answers.",
      "better_line": "Cast Rampaging Growth (4 mana) to create a 4/3 haste Insect, then cast Hunter's Insight (3 mana) targeting it, attack with the Insect into the mostly-tapped board to draw 4 cards and dig for survival options.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 195,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 123,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 2 life with no board, GPT53C Teach passed with 6 untapped lands when they could cast Rampaging Growth to create a 4/3 hasty creature, then cast Hunter's Insight on it, attack into an opponent with no untapped blockers (all opponent's creatures were either tapped or summoning sick), and draw 4 cards. This was their only out to find answers and they gave it up.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, effectively ending the turn without casting any spells.",
      "better_line": "Cast Rampaging Growth ({3}{G}) to create a 4/3 Insect with reach and haste, then cast Hunter's Insight ({2}{G}) targeting it, attack the opponent (no untapped non-sick blockers available), deal 4 damage and draw 4 cards to dig for answers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 197,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 124,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Ranger's Guile while Rampaging Growth is still on the stack, meaning the 4/3 land-creature hasn't been created yet. GPT53C Teach has no creatures on the battlefield to target with Ranger's Guile, so the spell likely fizzles. Even if it somehow resolves, spending mana and a card before the Rampaging Growth resolves is wasteful.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Ranger's Guile in response to their own Rampaging Growth, with no creatures on the battlefield to target.",
      "better_line": "Let Rampaging Growth resolve first, creating the 4/3 Insect land-creature, then potentially use Ranger's Guile on it for protection or the +1/+1 buff if needed. At 2 life, every resource matters.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 209,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 130,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "GPT53C Teach used Ranger's Guile on the animated Forest land to give it +1/+1 and hexproof, but Hunter's Edge was already going to deal 5 damage to the 5/4 Wildheart Invoker (killing it) without the extra power. The animated Forest ceases to be a creature at end of turn, so the +1/+1 counter is meaningless. At 2 life facing a wide board, Ranger's Guile could be critical for protecting a blocker from removal in future turns.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Ranger's Guile on the animated Forest for +1/+1 and hexproof, providing no meaningful benefit since Wildheart Invoker was already dying and the land animation expires at end of turn.",
      "better_line": "Save Ranger's Guile for a future turn where it could protect a crucial blocker from removal, which is vital at 2 life against a board full of attackers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 218,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 137,
    }
  ],
